@startuml 49-durable-run-restart
' Exactly-once across a crash: the outbox gives dispatch-at-least-once, the
' observation store gives apply-exactly-once (recovery.rs + orchestration.rs).
title Durable run across a restart — exactly-once effects (recovery.rs)
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FBFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #294C60
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF5FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #38789E
  LifeLineBorderColor #6A92AA
  GroupBackgroundColor #FFF3E8
  GroupBorderColor #D97638
}

participant "Kernel + recovery\nscheduler (embers)" as K #CDEACC
participant "F1r3drive\ncontinuation store" as S #E8DACB
participant "Validator\n(deploy · finality)" as V #FFE4A6

== forward execution (revision N) ==
K -> S : put EffectOutbox\n(sign the deploy once, INV-D6)
K -> V : deploy invoke_activity.rho

note over K, V #F8CECC
  ✖ process crashes here — before the observation is written,
  or after it but before advance_run. Either way the on-chain
  revision is still N and no command is claimed.
end note

== after restart — run_recovery_loop polls ==
K -> K : recover_runs_once: run is "running";\ntry_lock (non-blocking skip if busy, INV-T3)
K -> S : get RunRequest + Continuation (revision N)
S --> K : envelope (revision N)

group per pending effect — execute_activity
  K -> S : get Observation for effect_key?
  alt observation already stored (crash was after observing)
    S --> K : observation
    note right of K #FFF0C7
      Apply-exactly-once (INV-D5): the effect is
      not re-dispatched; its stored result is applied.
    end note
  else not observed (crash was during dispatch)
    S --> K : absent
    K -> S : get EffectOutbox
    S --> K : the same signed deploy
    K -> V : re-dispatch it\n(dispatch-at-least-once, INV-D6;\nidentical deploy id never lands twice)
    V --> K : finalized
    K -> S : put Observation
  end
  K -> K : apply_effect_observation
end

K -> S : put Continuation (revision N+1)
K -> V : advance_run CAS (expected_revision = N)
V --> K : finalized (revision N+1)

@enduml
